                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The Bureau of Near Eastern, South Asian, and African Affairs, under the direction
                    of Assistant Secretary of State McGhee, was created effective October 3, 1949.
                    The Division of Near Eastern Affairs ceased to exist and was replaced by the
                    Office of African and Near Eastern Affairs (ANE). Fraser Wilkins, at the same time, became Officer in Charge of
                    Palestine–Israel–Jordan Affairs in the new Office. The Department of State, the
                    following day, released a statement concerning these and other details of its
                    reorganization; for text, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, October 31, 1949, page 677.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
